  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">New Narratives 2022-2024</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">New Narratives 2022-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att st&#xe4;rka sj&#xe4;lvst&#xe4;ndig and kvalitativ journalistik i Liberia, genom att m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra f&#xf6;r New Narratives att bist&#xe5; med stipendier till journalister och kapacitets bygga liberianska mediahus. New Narratives kommer st&#xf6;tta nyhetsredaktioner med kapacitetsst&#xe4;rkning, journalist-stipendier och kompetensf&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkning fokuserat p&#xe5; digital mediaproduktion och f&#xf6;retagsutvecklande. Programmet syftar till att utrusta liberianska journalister och nyhetsredaktioner med resurser, know-how och st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r att kunna bedriva sj&#xe4;lvst&#xe4;ndig och gr&#xe4;vande journalistik.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution appraised here aims to strengthen independent and qualitative journalism in Liberia by supporting New Narratives to provide production grants to journalists and capacity build Liberian media houses. New Narratives will target newsrooms, with capacity building, journalism-grants and skills strengthening focused on digital media production and business support. The programme aims to equip Liberian journalists and news organisations with the resources, know-how and support to pursue independent and investigative reporting.

New Narratives overall goal is to strengthen local independent journalism in Liberia to actively contribute as part of a whole-of-society effort to combat corruption and support good governance and human rights. 

Two main outcomes are expected to be achieved by the intervention:

1) Liberian journalists are equipped with resources, know-how and support, including through strong relationships with relevant non-media CSOs, to pursue independent and investigative journalism during and after the project.

2) Liberian news organizations and New Narratives have the resources and know-how to enhance financial viability in a sustainable way to support investigative journalism.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">New Narratives overall goal is to strengthen local independent journalism in Liberia to actively contribute as part of a whole-of-society effort to combat corruption and support good governance and human rights. 

New Narratives are proposing to make a slight change to their first objective to reflect the new activities focused on War and Economic Crimes Court reporting. The overall goal continues to be to strengthen local independent journalism in Liberia to actively contribute as part of a whole-of-society effort to combat corruption and support good governance and human rights. 

With the new outcome, two main outcomes are expected to be achieved by the intervention:

1) Liberian journalists are equipped with resources, know-how and support, including through strong relationships with relevant non-media CSOs, to pursue independent and investigative journalism during and after the project,including on the war and economics crimes courts.  

2) Liberian news organizations and New Narratives have the resources and know-how to enhance financial viability in a sustainable way to support investigative journalism.

This will be achieved by the following broad activities, thoroughly outlined in the proposal, which each include a number of different outputs to promote and boost a sustainable investigative journalism ecosystem by:

a) Building strong investigative and independent journalism capacity; b) Building trusted news organizations with large reach and sustainable, independent revenue; c) Strengthening civil society collaborations; d) Offer investigative journalism grants to journalists at the concerned newsrooms</narrative>
  </description>
